1
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:53,030
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:55,960
[Episode 13]

3
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:30,430
My whole life

4
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:34,060
has been bitter as hell.

5
00:01:36,670 --> 00:01:38,020
I married a man

6
00:01:40,150 --> 00:01:41,570
who was even more reckless
than a black bear.

7
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:44,940
The only sweetness I ever had

8
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:46,840
came from you.

9
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:48,039
Hong,

10
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:52,900
does it really have to end this way?

11
00:02:03,370 --> 00:02:05,080
I was willing

12
00:02:05,230 --> 00:02:06,260
to end up here with you.

13
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:09,789
Being with you, even in death,

14
00:02:10,590 --> 00:02:12,310
feels better than being alive.

15
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:19,590
What if there's another way?

16
00:02:20,870 --> 00:02:22,470
Maybe...

17
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:25,190
There's no way left

18
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:27,370
for the two of us in this world.

19
00:02:29,030 --> 00:02:31,100
Let's go see
what's on the other side together.

20
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:35,030
It's pitch-black on the other side.

21
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:38,030
We can hold hands

22
00:02:38,710 --> 00:02:40,500
and light the way for each other,

23
00:02:41,060 --> 00:02:42,040
all right?

24
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:55,620
Hong,

25
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:57,420
your phone's ringing.

26
00:02:57,860 --> 00:02:59,490
Why don't you answer it first?

27
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:03,020
Don't answer it.

28
00:03:03,530 --> 00:03:04,150
Answer it.

29
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,310
What if it's something urgent?

30
00:03:06,810 --> 00:03:08,840
It can't be anything important.

31
00:03:18,710 --> 00:03:19,240
Hello,

32
00:03:19,590 --> 00:03:20,430
is this Chen Hong?

33
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,530
This is the police station calling.

34
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:23,800
Your father-in-law is in the hospital.

35
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,050
You need to come over right away.

36
00:03:38,370 --> 00:03:39,500
Bin.

37
00:03:42,870 --> 00:03:44,780
Are you a relative of Li Bin?

38
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:49,620
What happened to my father-in-law?

39
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:52,250
Your father-in-law
had an episode at the station.

40
00:03:52,250 --> 00:03:53,860
The two of us brought him here
in our patrol car right away.

41
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:55,220
We didn't waste any time on the way.

42
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:56,150
That's true.

43
00:03:57,180 --> 00:03:57,800
Doctor,

44
00:03:58,180 --> 00:03:59,660
what's wrong with him?

45
00:03:59,930 --> 00:04:00,810
He suffered a sudden stroke.

46
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:03,140
Thanks to these two officers
bringing him in in time,

47
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:04,430
his life was saved.

48
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:06,020
He's still unconscious.

49
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:07,240
Can he still wake up?

50
00:04:07,870 --> 00:04:09,870
The area of ischemic brain damage
is too extensive.

51
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:11,220
There's only a 30% - 40% chance

52
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:12,400
he'll regain consciousness.

53
00:04:13,070 --> 00:04:14,420
Even if he does wake up,

54
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:16,329
he'll most likely
be paralyzed on one side.

55
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:17,660
His speech and mobility

56
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:18,740
will both be affected.

57
00:04:19,070 --> 00:04:20,100
What does that mean?

58
00:04:21,190 --> 00:04:22,510
We'll have to keep monitoring him.

59
00:04:22,510 --> 00:04:23,060
Doctor,

60
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:24,920
given his condition,

61
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,390
he won't end up
in a vegetative state, will he?

62
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:28,370
Bin.

63
00:04:28,930 --> 00:04:29,660
Bin!

64
00:04:30,310 --> 00:04:31,270
Bin...

65
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:32,630
-Don't scare me.
-Please stay calm, ma'am.

66
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:33,430
Bin...

67
00:04:33,430 --> 00:04:34,010
Please, try not to get too worked up.

68
00:04:34,010 --> 00:04:35,000
Officer,

69
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:38,100
did my father-in-law say anything?

70
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:39,510
He didn't say anything.

71
00:04:39,510 --> 00:04:41,120
He collapsed as soon as he walked in

72
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:42,560
and hit his head hard enough to bleed.

73
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,890
Bin... Bin...

74
00:04:47,890 --> 00:04:49,100
Please, don't scare me.

75
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,750
Bin, open your eyes.

76
00:04:50,750 --> 00:04:52,770
Please. Listen to me.

77
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,040
Bin...

78
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:24,740
Bin.

79
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:26,230
Bin!

80
00:05:26,250 --> 00:05:27,340
Where does it hurt?

81
00:05:27,450 --> 00:05:28,070
Doctor.

82
00:05:33,310 --> 00:05:34,720
The patient is responding normally
to external stimuli,

83
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,470
which means he's regained consciousness.

84
00:05:37,770 --> 00:05:40,330
So when will he be able to speak?

85
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:41,740
Let's keep monitoring him for now.

86
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:43,430
The doctor says you're going to be okay.

87
00:05:43,430 --> 00:05:45,860
Stay calm. Stay calm, okay?

88
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:47,659
You heard the doctor.

89
00:05:47,810 --> 00:05:49,180
You're going to be okay.

90
00:05:49,770 --> 00:05:50,710
Don't get excited.

91
00:05:58,220 --> 00:06:00,260
He's not gonna bite you, anyway. Hurry up.

92
00:06:06,510 --> 00:06:07,620
Thanks, guys.

93
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:21,000
Watch the road.

94
00:06:23,730 --> 00:06:24,440
Dad,

95
00:06:24,930 --> 00:06:26,870
I found a housekeeper for you.

96
00:06:26,870 --> 00:06:28,270
She'll take care of you and Mom,

97
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:30,690
and help me look after Qiu, too.

98
00:06:32,290 --> 00:06:33,510
With Dewu gone,

99
00:06:33,510 --> 00:06:35,300
there's a ton of work left at the factory,

100
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:37,360
so I'll be tied up for a while.

101
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:39,310
But don't worry.

102
00:06:39,310 --> 00:06:41,040
I'll come home
and check on you every day.

103
00:06:45,930 --> 00:06:47,010
Given your condition,

104
00:06:47,430 --> 00:06:48,630
there's no point in lying to you.

105
00:06:49,250 --> 00:06:50,870
Dewu really wasn't killed
by the two of us.

106
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,659
I want to know who killed him, too.

107
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:55,980
I owe that person a big thank-you.

108
00:07:11,310 --> 00:07:12,430
I shouldn't have listened to you.

109
00:07:12,430 --> 00:07:13,560
We didn't find a damn thing all day,

110
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:15,060
and 8 hot dogs are gone.

111
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,130
Are you reimbursing me for those?

112
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:17,930
I told you to borrow a police dog.

113
00:07:17,930 --> 00:07:18,870
What did you borrow?

114
00:07:18,870 --> 00:07:20,450
That police dog outranks me.

115
00:07:20,450 --> 00:07:21,920
It's not like I can just borrow it
whenever I want.

116
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,750
Where the hell could that hand have gone?

117
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:26,430
It's driving me crazy.

118
00:07:26,430 --> 00:07:27,410
It's so frustrating.

119
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:31,760
What are you doing?

120
00:07:32,250 --> 00:07:33,810
Eating cold steamed buns
in the middle of winter?

121
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:36,520
Just having a little something
to tide me over.

122
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,270
Have something warm.

123
00:07:41,310 --> 00:07:42,950
What's that smell on you?

124
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:47,300
What are you doing?

125
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:48,830
What's that smell?

126
00:07:48,830 --> 00:07:50,159
What smell?

127
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:51,720
Are you...

128
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,390
Move your hand.

129
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,750
What are you doing?

130
00:07:54,750 --> 00:07:55,430
Move your hand!

131
00:07:55,430 --> 00:07:57,420
I'm your sister.
Can't I see what you're hiding?

132
00:07:58,500 --> 00:07:58,980
Move your hand!

133
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,210
Is that perfume?

134
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:24,170
You're seeing someone, aren't you?

135
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:29,160
Seriously?

136
00:08:29,420 --> 00:08:30,770
Is she from Tiecheng or out of town?

137
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:32,390
We'll talk tonight.

138
00:08:32,390 --> 00:08:33,549
-I have something to do.
-W-What does she do for a living?

139
00:08:33,549 --> 00:08:34,340
We'll talk tonight.

140
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:34,789
Don't wait until tonight.

141
00:08:34,789 --> 00:08:36,240
Bring her home so I can meet her.

142
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:36,480
I know.

143
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,270
We could have a meal or something.

144
00:08:37,270 --> 00:08:37,950
I have something to take care of.

145
00:08:38,370 --> 00:08:38,770
I'm leaving.

146
00:08:38,770 --> 00:08:39,720
Don't keep acting so scatterbrained.

147
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:41,360
Why don't you tell me anything anymore?

148
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:43,440
What on earth
does she see in you? Honestly.

149
00:08:48,050 --> 00:08:49,290
Always worrying about you.

150
00:08:49,790 --> 00:08:50,890
Why don't you worry about something
that actually matters?

151
00:08:58,220 --> 00:09:00,460
Qianqian's gotten so picky with food.

152
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:01,870
I don't even know what
to make for her anymore.

153
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:07,940
Think about it.

154
00:09:07,940 --> 00:09:09,170
What should we have for dinner tonight?

155
00:09:17,510 --> 00:09:18,720
How about pig's trotters?

156
00:09:18,910 --> 00:09:20,240
Qianqian might like them.

157
00:09:21,030 --> 00:09:22,570
All right. Take them out to thaw.

158
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:23,550
Let's braise them in soy sauce
and sugar for her.

159
00:09:23,550 --> 00:09:24,830
She likes sweet flavors.

160
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:25,820
Okay.

161
00:10:02,470 --> 00:10:04,740
Why does it smell
like pig's trotters in here?

162
00:10:06,570 --> 00:10:11,170
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall]

163
00:10:08,370 --> 00:10:09,250
I heard

164
00:10:09,650 --> 00:10:11,120
the cigarette butt

165
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,790
kept glowing, then going out,

166
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:15,890
then glowing again, then going out again.

167
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:19,480
That Zhao guy smoked all night,

168
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:21,000
yet somehow couldn't finish
a single cigarette.

169
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:24,140
When the police found him
the next morning,

170
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:24,980
guess what?

171
00:10:24,980 --> 00:10:25,440
What?

172
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,240
What happened?

173
00:10:26,790 --> 00:10:27,840
Come on, tell us.

174
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,910
The cigarette hadn't burned down at all.

175
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:33,630
It was like someone had been
pouring human oil on it all night.

176
00:10:33,630 --> 00:10:34,770
Isn't that creepy?

177
00:10:35,770 --> 00:10:37,240
Seriously?

178
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:38,310
Yeah, really.

179
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:39,270
Who told you that?

180
00:10:39,290 --> 00:10:41,170
Mr. Wang's wife told me herself.

181
00:10:41,790 --> 00:10:44,770
She said it was sometime
after midnight the night before last.

182
00:10:44,770 --> 00:10:46,740
Mr. Wang was passing by the square

183
00:10:47,150 --> 00:10:49,620
when his arm suddenly went numb

184
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:51,010
and his back started to feel heavy.

185
00:10:51,010 --> 00:10:52,910
He went home and came down
with a fever of over 39°C.

186
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:55,670
He lay in bed,
crying out that he was cold

187
00:10:55,690 --> 00:10:56,910
and that his arm hurt,

188
00:10:57,370 --> 00:10:58,510
just howling in pain.

189
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,740
Looks like Li Dewu was buried yesterday,

190
00:11:01,740 --> 00:11:03,170
and the evil energy
still hasn't dispersed.

191
00:11:03,170 --> 00:11:04,220
No kidding.

192
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:05,860
Now that you mention it,

193
00:11:06,910 --> 00:11:08,560
why does my arm feel weird too?

194
00:11:08,630 --> 00:11:13,550
[Welcome]

195
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:10,340
I need to leave early today.

196
00:11:10,870 --> 00:11:11,790
Okay, sir.

197
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:18,820
What are we gonna do?

198
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,320
This place is huge,

199
00:11:23,170 --> 00:11:24,390
and there's not a single customer here.

200
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,870
How am I supposed
to keep this business running?

201
00:11:30,270 --> 00:11:30,870
Dong,

202
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:32,610
I already chewed out the people under me.

203
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:35,150
Even with no customers, they still need
to keep themselves sharp and presentable.

204
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,500
And then there are those who took leave.

205
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:42,290
What are we men out here
trying to make a living supposed to fear?

206
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,720
Going hungry is even scarier.

207
00:11:45,630 --> 00:11:46,650
Dong, you know,

208
00:11:47,620 --> 00:11:48,890
apart from me,

209
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,170
the people around you

210
00:11:50,170 --> 00:11:51,290
have rather desperate (disparate) levels
of education.

211
00:11:52,510 --> 00:11:55,290
They keep gossiping down there,
saying all sorts of ignorant things.

212
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:58,630
What did Ms. Wan say?

213
00:11:58,660 --> 00:11:59,800
Nothing.

214
00:11:59,870 --> 00:12:00,880
You know why?

215
00:12:03,050 --> 00:12:04,940
Because you're not sincere.

216
00:12:05,410 --> 00:12:10,450
[Welcome]

217
00:12:13,290 --> 00:12:15,120
-Welcome, Ms. Wan.
-Welcome, Ms. Wan.

218
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:21,800
Let's see what we've got here.

219
00:12:51,910 --> 00:12:52,940
There's something sinister over there.

220
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:54,340
Something what?

221
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:55,300
Come on, come on.

222
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:05,520
When elevator...

223
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:08,110
faces elevator,

224
00:13:09,250 --> 00:13:12,460
qi won't stay, so luck won't remain.

225
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,690
Too many women, too few men,

226
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:22,190
yin takes over, the home can't sustain.

227
00:13:22,270 --> 00:13:24,190
A crystal chandelier above

228
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:26,690
brings trouble and blocks the road.

229
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:28,910
A golden leopard crouching in the hall

230
00:13:28,930 --> 00:13:31,580
bares its fangs and keeps wealth away.

231
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:33,740
Ms. Wan,

232
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:35,890
if we do everything you say,

233
00:13:36,510 --> 00:13:38,350
won't I have
to tear this whole place apart?

234
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:40,180
What are you talking about?

235
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,770
Why do you think I came here?

236
00:13:42,290 --> 00:13:44,120
To get big things done
with a little money, of course.

237
00:13:44,830 --> 00:13:46,480
Here, take this.

238
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:49,970
Just put one in each private room.

239
00:13:51,610 --> 00:13:52,570
How much is this gonna cost?

240
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,620
What are you talking about? No charge.

241
00:13:55,370 --> 00:13:56,360
Just consider it a wish
for your business to prosper.

242
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:56,890
That's all.

243
00:13:57,980 --> 00:13:58,920
I'm heading back.

244
00:13:59,690 --> 00:14:00,390
What?

245
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:04,670
How much?

246
00:14:07,530 --> 00:14:08,270
Seriously?

247
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,000
The great immortal behind me says

248
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,030
I can't take no money for it.

249
00:14:16,390 --> 00:14:17,460
Give me anything from 8,000 yuan

250
00:14:17,670 --> 00:14:18,460
to under 9,000 yuan.

251
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:19,280
Whatever you think is fair.

252
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:19,820
Of course.

253
00:14:19,820 --> 00:14:21,210
I-I have to pay you.

254
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:22,250
How about this?

255
00:14:22,330 --> 00:14:23,420
Is 8,800 yuan okay?

256
00:14:23,670 --> 00:14:25,530
Sure. We could both
use a little good luck.

257
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:28,120
Put this one

258
00:14:28,530 --> 00:14:30,310
in that private room,

259
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:32,010
under the sofa or somewhere.

260
00:14:32,390 --> 00:14:33,420
What the hell is that?

261
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:37,500
This place

262
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:38,770
has too much yin energy.

263
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:40,000
Well...

264
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:41,760
looks like I won't be leaving
anytime soon.

265
00:14:44,130 --> 00:14:44,870
Ms. Wan,

266
00:14:46,090 --> 00:14:46,800
have some tea.

267
00:14:51,580 --> 00:14:52,250
Ms. Wan,

268
00:14:53,790 --> 00:14:55,460
would you mind telling us

269
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:57,830
what exactly you saw just now?

270
00:15:01,540 --> 00:15:02,310
Damn,

271
00:15:03,670 --> 00:15:05,220
it's an outsider.

272
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:07,500
W-What do you mean, an outsider?

273
00:15:09,670 --> 00:15:10,910
Let me put it this way.

274
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:14,150
The great immortal behind me

275
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:16,130
is also an outsider.

276
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:19,440
Ever since it found my mother,

277
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:20,700
then passed down to me,

278
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:23,080
it must have been with us
for over 50 years.

279
00:15:23,580 --> 00:15:25,360
Now, a new one has come to Yuhong Square,

280
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:27,500
and it wants

281
00:15:28,530 --> 00:15:29,390
to establish

282
00:15:30,630 --> 00:15:32,170
itself here.

283
00:15:33,410 --> 00:15:34,820
To establish itself here,

284
00:15:34,820 --> 00:15:35,940
it needs to burn incense.

285
00:15:36,250 --> 00:15:37,740
And each stick of incense

286
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:40,030
requires a human life.

287
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:43,790
So the two people
who died the other day...

288
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:45,600
that means two sticks of incense, right?

289
00:15:46,430 --> 00:15:48,940
And if human lives are being used
as incense,

290
00:15:49,030 --> 00:15:50,620
the victims can't be ordinary people.

291
00:15:50,910 --> 00:15:51,860
Think about it.

292
00:15:52,390 --> 00:15:54,120
Zhao Changyou and Li Dewu—

293
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:56,930
weren't they both well-known figures
in Tiecheng?

294
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,170
No kidding.

295
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:01,410
Zhao Changyou used to come
to our dance hall all the time.

296
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:03,720
He'd spend thousands every time.

297
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:05,700
Dong, what kind of car did he drive?

298
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:07,120
An Audi, right?

299
00:16:09,100 --> 00:16:10,220
And then there's Li Dewu.

300
00:16:10,300 --> 00:16:12,100
He was one of the wealthiest people

301
00:16:12,130 --> 00:16:13,470
in Tiecheng.

302
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:16,870
For this incense offering,

303
00:16:17,050 --> 00:16:18,620
there need to be three sticks.

304
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:20,400
If you ask me,

305
00:16:21,070 --> 00:16:23,180
another life is going to be taken.

306
00:16:23,870 --> 00:16:25,770
This person

307
00:16:25,770 --> 00:16:27,620
has to be well-known,

308
00:16:28,050 --> 00:16:29,130
with a strong enough fate.

309
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:30,360
Only then

310
00:16:30,820 --> 00:16:31,910
can the new one establish itself.

311
00:16:36,410 --> 00:16:37,820
Think about that...

312
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:40,050
It needs three sticks of incense...

313
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:44,890
Three sticks of incense.

314
00:16:58,050 --> 00:16:59,160
Just wait.

315
00:17:01,030 --> 00:17:02,230
I'm coming.

316
00:17:11,349 --> 00:17:12,420
Ms. Wan, y-you...

317
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,480
is it coming after me now?

318
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:15,650
Have a look at it, please.

319
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:24,420
This...

320
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:26,900
it's nothing.

321
00:17:27,250 --> 00:17:29,330
Maybe one of your guys is playing a prank.

322
00:17:31,090 --> 00:17:32,270
Y-You think so?

323
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:34,820
Well... you never know.

324
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:38,410
Have you ever seen this before?

325
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:42,890
What kind of great immortal

326
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:44,110
would write such notes?

327
00:17:44,770 --> 00:17:45,880
I don't buy it.

328
00:17:45,880 --> 00:17:46,920
Write it down now.

329
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:48,050
All of you, write it down.

330
00:17:50,850 --> 00:17:52,400
Check this properly.

331
00:17:59,070 --> 00:17:59,510
That one...

332
00:17:59,910 --> 00:18:02,730
[Just wait. I'm coming.]

333
00:18:02,070 --> 00:18:02,880
This isn't the one.

334
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:04,160
Go, go, go.

335
00:18:08,070 --> 00:18:11,260
[You]

336
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:22,920
[You]

337
00:18:30,530 --> 00:18:31,330
[You]

338
00:18:33,770 --> 00:18:34,850
You don't even know how to write
the character for "wait"

339
00:18:34,850 --> 00:18:35,930
and had to use pinyin instead?

340
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:37,880
Even if you wrote it in pinyin,
it should be the third tone.

341
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:38,790
How did you end up

342
00:18:38,790 --> 00:18:39,980
writing the first tone?

343
00:18:39,980 --> 00:18:41,380
You actually wrote it with your accent,
didn't you?

344
00:18:42,910 --> 00:18:44,110
What are you laughing at?

345
00:18:45,810 --> 00:18:46,940
This is scary.

346
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,810
Have the people outside write too.

347
00:19:01,050 --> 00:19:02,310
Zhao Changyou

348
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:05,250
wasn't the only one who came just now.

349
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:07,340
I just vaguely saw

350
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:09,870
what happened that night.

351
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:11,640
Zhao Changyou

352
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:14,060
was sitting right there,

353
00:19:15,270 --> 00:19:16,180
and there was

354
00:19:17,050 --> 00:19:18,670
a young man next to him.

355
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:20,050
Dong,

356
00:19:20,870 --> 00:19:21,700
I'm here.

357
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:29,080
How did you get in again?

358
00:19:29,470 --> 00:19:30,680
No one stopped me downstairs.

359
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:40,410
What the hell is that?
